1
00:00:48,910 --> 00:00:53,010
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,270 --> 00:00:55,910
[Episode 18]

3
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:59,800
[Golden Imperial Dance Hall]

4
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:57,960
Alright, Dong.

5
00:00:57,960 --> 00:00:58,850
You have fun.

6
00:00:58,850 --> 00:01:00,100
I'm off now.

7
00:01:00,350 --> 00:01:01,070
Alright.

8
00:01:09,289 --> 00:01:09,900
Yang.

9
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:14,090
Dong's business
hasn't been good lately.

10
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:16,480
And he only uses his trusted men.

11
00:01:17,350 --> 00:01:18,450
I've been with him for years

12
00:01:18,450 --> 00:01:20,200
before he let me sell the cigarettes.

13
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:22,600
He really doesn't
take on new guys anymore.

14
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:32,000
You taking on guys?

15
00:01:35,030 --> 00:01:36,890
Are you that desperate for money?

16
00:01:37,090 --> 00:01:39,220
Camel six, 555 eight, Mild Seven twelve.

17
00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:40,300
Camel, six yuan.

18
00:01:40,340 --> 00:01:41,340
555, eight yuan.

19
00:01:41,710 --> 00:01:42,850
Marlboro, thirteen yuan.

20
00:01:42,850 --> 00:01:44,180
Dunhill, fifteen yuan.

21
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:46,460
Which one is thirteen?

22
00:01:49,430 --> 00:01:50,229
Dunhill.

23
00:01:50,759 --> 00:01:51,930
Dunhill, fifteen.

24
00:01:51,930 --> 00:01:53,039
Marlboro, thirteen.

25
00:01:53,039 --> 00:01:53,539
Dunhill, fifteen.

26
00:01:53,539 --> 00:01:56,070
Go to the entrance
of Imperial Seafood later.

27
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:57,650
A lot of people treat guests there.

28
00:01:57,650 --> 00:01:59,580
Try to get them to buy by the carton.

29
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:00,650
Page me.

30
00:02:01,430 --> 00:02:02,890
I'll bring the goods over.

31
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:04,730
What if something goes wrong?

32
00:02:04,730 --> 00:02:05,860
I'll drop your name.

33
00:02:08,250 --> 00:02:09,050
What's wrong?

34
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:10,840
Why mention me?

35
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:12,650
If you drop my name, I'll get beaten up.

36
00:02:12,650 --> 00:02:14,430
Aren't you my boss now?

37
00:02:15,710 --> 00:02:16,829
You are my dad.

38
00:02:16,850 --> 00:02:18,090
Don't say that.

39
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:19,150
If the cops catch you,

40
00:02:19,150 --> 00:02:20,930
you'd mention me first too, huh?

41
00:02:20,930 --> 00:02:22,370
No, no, definitely not.

42
00:02:22,590 --> 00:02:23,240
Run.

43
00:02:24,579 --> 00:02:25,470
Run, run, run.

44
00:02:26,190 --> 00:02:27,250
Wait, wait, wait.

45
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,720
Take this for self-defense.

46
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,090
If someone starts trouble...

47
00:02:35,090 --> 00:02:36,030
Stab him.

48
00:02:37,790 --> 00:02:38,680
Wrong again?

49
00:02:38,970 --> 00:02:40,530
We are out here to make money.

50
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:41,650
Safety first.

51
00:02:44,190 --> 00:02:46,190
You can't actually stab anyone, Yang.

52
00:02:46,190 --> 00:02:46,970
Don't worry.

53
00:02:48,079 --> 00:02:49,150
Repeat after me.

54
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:50,520
Dunhill, fifteen.

55
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:51,190
Marlboro, thirteen.

56
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:52,530
Don't actually stab anyone.

57
00:02:52,530 --> 00:02:53,760
Don't actually stab anyone.

58
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:54,260
Right.

59
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:57,770
Give this to your sister.

60
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:00,410
Where did you get this?

61
00:03:01,190 --> 00:03:01,990
Don't ask.

62
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:03,080
Just give it to her.

63
00:03:10,710 --> 00:03:12,570
Hey buddy, want some cigarettes?

64
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:15,840
Sir.

65
00:03:16,410 --> 00:03:17,620
Want some cigarettes?

66
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:18,560
I've got foreign smokes.

67
00:03:18,430 --> 00:03:21,470
[Banquet Hall] [To the parking lot]
[Dragon Palace Seafood Restaurant]

68
00:03:18,810 --> 00:03:19,910
They're all good.

69
00:03:19,910 --> 00:03:20,630
If you want some,

70
00:03:20,630 --> 00:03:21,710
I'll give you a discount.

71
00:03:21,710 --> 00:03:24,860
These smokes will make you
look classy at the dinner table.

72
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:25,920
Sir, wait a minute.

73
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,140
How about this?

74
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,730
I'll give you this one for free.

75
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:32,079
Try it. It's good.

76
00:03:38,210 --> 00:03:38,970
How much?

77
00:03:39,090 --> 00:03:40,090
Twenty.

78
00:03:40,090 --> 00:03:41,060
Too expensive.

79
00:03:41,770 --> 00:03:42,410
Come on, man.

80
00:03:42,410 --> 00:03:44,250
Marlboros all go for this price.

81
00:03:47,079 --> 00:03:48,040
Thanks, man.

82
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:59,480
That's all I've got. Take it or leave it.

83
00:04:00,330 --> 00:04:01,830
[Banquet Hall] [To the parking lot]
[Dragon Palace Seafood Restaurant]

84
00:04:39,090 --> 00:04:39,810
Be careful.

85
00:04:39,810 --> 00:04:40,560
It's fine.

86
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:41,130
Let's go.

87
00:04:41,430 --> 00:04:42,830
T-T-Then, from now on,

88
00:04:42,830 --> 00:04:45,210
the bulk lubricant from your factory...

89
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:46,150
Don't worry.

90
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:47,510
From now on,

91
00:04:47,510 --> 00:04:48,659
we'll buy it from you.

92
00:04:48,659 --> 00:04:49,130
Really?

93
00:04:49,130 --> 00:04:50,220
We'll sign the contract tomorrow,

94
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:50,680
okay?

95
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:51,500
Keep your word.

96
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:53,000
I will. No problem.

97
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:53,500
Come on.

98
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:54,800
Easy, easy.

99
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:55,850
I'm leaving.

100
00:04:56,860 --> 00:04:57,390
Careful.

101
00:04:57,630 --> 00:04:58,190
Bye.

102
00:05:20,830 --> 00:05:21,510
Drive.

103
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:00,120
Young man.

104
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:01,750
Calm down.

105
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:04,100
If you want money,

106
00:06:04,830 --> 00:06:06,890
I have a few hundred in my bag. Take it.

107
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:07,680
This car—

108
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:09,640
drive it away if you want.

109
00:06:10,750 --> 00:06:12,430
It's not worth it, really.

110
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:14,800
You think you're brushing off a beggar?

111
00:06:16,540 --> 00:06:17,480
These days,

112
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:19,510
it's not easy to make money.

113
00:06:20,370 --> 00:06:22,100
I'm just pretending to be rich.

114
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:24,900
I really don't have that much.

115
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:30,920
If you don't have that much,

116
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:33,580
how could you hire someone
to kill your husband?

117
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,370
Who are you?

118
00:06:43,870 --> 00:06:46,670
Pan Jinlian at least
left Wu Dalang a whole corpse.

119
00:06:47,250 --> 00:06:49,450
You're more ruthless than Pan Jinlian.

120
00:06:49,810 --> 00:06:52,070
Pan Jinlian was a good person in history.

121
00:06:52,430 --> 00:06:53,570
The books are all rumors.

122
00:06:53,570 --> 00:06:54,770
Are you a good person?

123
00:06:56,770 --> 00:06:58,240
You're waving a knife around.

124
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,700
You're a good person, huh?

125
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:15,640
Give me the money and I'll let you go.

126
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:18,010
Your business has nothing to do with me.

127
00:07:23,890 --> 00:07:25,020
How much do you want?

128
00:07:28,390 --> 00:07:29,070
100,000.

129
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:33,600
You might as well stab me to death.

130
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:36,420
Where am I supposed
to get 100,000 for you?

131
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:37,880
Why don't you go rob a bank?

132
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:39,100
The cops already said

133
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:40,740
Li Dewu's death
has nothing to do with me.

134
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:41,870
It was an accident.

135
00:07:49,159 --> 00:07:50,680
What if the cops find out

136
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:52,600
it was Wang Liye who paid Dong

137
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,950
to take Li Dewu out?

138
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:01,200
Does Wang Liye
have anything to do with you?

139
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:11,030
Just stab me to death.

140
00:08:11,250 --> 00:08:12,980
I don't think you want me to live anyway.

141
00:08:12,980 --> 00:08:13,920
Is it worth it?

142
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:15,070
You went to all that trouble.

143
00:08:15,070 --> 00:08:16,300
Was Li Dewu your dad?

144
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:17,300
Money is my dad.

145
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:18,740
I only care about money.

146
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:20,550
What if you never stop?

147
00:08:21,060 --> 00:08:22,890
Today you need money
and ask me for 100,000.

148
00:08:22,890 --> 00:08:24,860
Tomorrow you need food
and ask me for 100,000.

149
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:26,100
And later you'll ask me for 100,000

150
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:26,870
to get a wife and have kids.

151
00:08:26,870 --> 00:08:28,190
I'm not a bank!

152
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:39,440
-Help!
-Stop shouting!

153
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:40,220
-Help!
-Stop shouting!

154
00:08:40,220 --> 00:08:40,770
Stop shouting!

155
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:41,650
-Help!
-Stop shouting!

156
00:08:41,650 --> 00:08:42,549
-Help!
-Stop shouting!

157
00:08:42,549 --> 00:08:43,750
Shout again and I'll—

158
00:08:44,169 --> 00:08:45,110
Don't hit me.

159
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:46,240
Don't hit me.

160
00:08:46,370 --> 00:08:46,840
Don't move!

161
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:48,270
-Don't hit me.
-I'm telling you!

162
00:08:48,270 --> 00:08:49,290
Don't think I won't kill you!

163
00:08:49,290 --> 00:08:50,250
I'll tell you the truth.

164
00:08:50,250 --> 00:08:52,580
I'm the one
who chopped off Li Dewu's hand.

165
00:09:09,030 --> 00:09:10,090
You chopped it off?

166
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:11,630
I chopped it off.

167
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:19,450
He used that hand to beat me every day.

168
00:09:29,170 --> 00:09:30,200
I don't hit women.

169
00:10:09,170 --> 00:10:11,830
If you say you've killed someone,
I believe you.

170
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:13,990
But if you say you've been with a woman,

171
00:10:14,490 --> 00:10:15,950
I really don't believe it.

172
00:10:20,910 --> 00:10:21,910
Give me the money.

173
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:24,290
From now on,
we have nothing to do with each other.

174
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:25,220
Otherwise I'll—

175
00:10:28,250 --> 00:10:29,850
Otherwise, what will you do?

176
00:10:31,270 --> 00:10:32,220
Call the cops?

177
00:10:33,550 --> 00:10:36,390
Tell them I hired you to kill Li Dewu?

178
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:38,940
Or tell them

179
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:40,460
you robbed and raped me?

180
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:47,860
If you want money, earn it yourself.

181
00:10:48,890 --> 00:10:50,550
Come work for me at my company.

182
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:52,750
I'll pay you a high salary.

183
00:10:53,510 --> 00:10:55,390
You can earn 100,000 legally.

184
00:11:05,940 --> 00:11:07,270
Aren't you afraid of me?

185
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:11,010
Why would I be afraid of you?

186
00:11:12,270 --> 00:11:13,460
We're the same kind.

187
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:16,900
We'd do whatever it takes to survive.

188
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:50,120
My clothes are dirty.

189
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:51,780
Help me get them dry-cleaned.

190
00:11:58,800 --> 00:11:59,660
[Fire Hydrant]

191
00:12:01,740 --> 00:12:03,600
Liu, I forgot to tell you.

192
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:05,080
There's a dinner party tonight.

193
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:06,530
The restaurant needs this wine,

194
00:12:06,530 --> 00:12:08,530
so you have to move it back to the car.

195
00:12:13,620 --> 00:12:14,950
What are you staring at?

196
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:16,130
Move it.

197
00:12:29,410 --> 00:12:30,850
Why aren't you eating?

198
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,630
Mom, this doesn't taste good.

199
00:12:35,030 --> 00:12:36,030
Then what do you want to eat?

200
00:12:36,030 --> 00:12:37,750
I want a hamburger.

201
00:12:39,130 --> 00:12:39,910
I want KFC.

202
00:12:39,910 --> 00:12:40,870
I want KFC.

203
00:12:40,870 --> 00:12:42,330
I want KFC.

204
00:12:42,350 --> 00:12:43,690
I want KFC.

205
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:48,110
[Fire Hydrant]

206
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:57,850
-I want KFC.
-You want KFC, huh?

207
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:17,140
Tell me how Li Dewu died.

208
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:29,530
The more detailed, the better.

209
00:13:35,450 --> 00:13:39,050
[Limin Bookstore] [Cashier]

210
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:41,370
I've got something to do.

211
00:13:41,370 --> 00:13:42,480
Keep this envelope safe.

212
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:45,740
[Limin Bookstore] [Cashier]

213
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:44,480
I'll pick you up after work tonight.

214
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:27,240
That job Liu Yang found,

215
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:28,150
how's the pay?

216
00:14:30,910 --> 00:14:33,110
He's working for the late Li Dewu's wife

217
00:14:33,510 --> 00:14:35,040
who's always making a fuss.

218
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:37,720
She orders Yang around for everything.

219
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:38,780
Pays well, though.

220
00:14:38,870 --> 00:14:39,510
But

221
00:14:39,910 --> 00:14:41,710
he's gotta watch his pager 24/7,

222
00:14:42,100 --> 00:14:43,230
on call all the time.

223
00:14:43,790 --> 00:14:45,600
She treats Yang like a eunuch.

224
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:49,250
His boss is Chen Hong?

225
00:14:50,150 --> 00:14:53,280
Their driver chopped off
her husband's hand and ran off.

226
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:58,030
If you ask me,

227
00:14:58,910 --> 00:15:00,150
Yang doing this job

228
00:15:01,630 --> 00:15:02,840
is a waste of his

229
00:15:03,750 --> 00:15:05,410
railway school diploma.

230
00:15:06,510 --> 00:15:07,670
Driving for a widow,

231
00:15:07,910 --> 00:15:09,150
isn't it bad luck?

232
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:11,890
I asked him.

233
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:13,150
I said,

234
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:16,150
"What are you getting out of this?"

235
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:19,510
He said he wants to save more money.

236
00:15:20,290 --> 00:15:23,350
I said, "You're saving up
to get married and have kids?"

237
00:15:24,150 --> 00:15:25,340
Guess what he said.

238
00:15:27,650 --> 00:15:29,250
He said, "Chen Hong paged me.

239
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:30,720
I gotta go."

240
00:15:30,890 --> 00:15:32,420
What kind of answer is that?

241
00:15:43,770 --> 00:15:44,370
Come here.

242
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:47,060
Waiting for me to page you?

243
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:48,220
Hurry up.

244
00:15:52,270 --> 00:15:53,600
Which one looks better?

245
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,320
To go with this skirt.

246
00:15:58,670 --> 00:15:59,400
I don't know.

247
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:03,460
This one.

248
00:16:03,710 --> 00:16:04,290
Okay.

249
00:16:06,010 --> 00:16:08,320
Ma'am, look how nice your husband is.

250
00:16:09,030 --> 00:16:09,840
He just stands there

251
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:10,910
without saying a word.

252
00:16:10,910 --> 00:16:12,130
Any other husband

253
00:16:12,130 --> 00:16:13,630
would've gotten annoyed by now.

254
00:16:13,630 --> 00:16:15,150
He's been shopping with you all day

255
00:16:15,150 --> 00:16:16,460
and hasn't complained about going back.

256
00:16:16,460 --> 00:16:17,670
You can buy whatever you want.

257
00:16:17,670 --> 00:16:18,960
How did you train him?

258
00:16:21,220 --> 00:16:22,550
This one's nice.

259
00:16:25,700 --> 00:16:26,390
Go try it on.

260
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:28,460
I don't want it.

261
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:30,860
I'm not buying it for you.

262
00:16:31,250 --> 00:16:33,450
You represent my image when you're out.

263
00:16:33,550 --> 00:16:34,960
If people see you looking sloppy,

264
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:36,420
who are you embarrassing?

265
00:16:37,220 --> 00:16:38,280
I'll take this one.

266
00:16:52,010 --> 00:16:52,720
Thanks.

267
00:17:04,349 --> 00:17:06,010
Have a bite. I can't finish it.

268
00:17:07,589 --> 00:17:10,390
Just eat it when I tell you to.
Don't be so stubborn.

269
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:22,730
Let's go.

270
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:24,420
You must dance with me.

271
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:25,750
The drinks went straight to my head.

272
00:17:25,750 --> 00:17:27,010
I can't dance anymore.

273
00:17:27,290 --> 00:17:28,530
I already booked the place.

274
00:17:28,530 --> 00:17:29,530
Are you not showing me respect?

275
00:17:29,530 --> 00:17:30,070
No, it's not that.

276
00:17:30,070 --> 00:17:31,770
It's not that I'm not showing you respect.

277
00:17:31,770 --> 00:17:33,420
My child's waiting at home.

278
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:34,570
Who doesn't have a child?

279
00:17:34,570 --> 00:17:35,900
Come on, that's enough.

280
00:17:36,070 --> 00:17:38,030
I just like women with children.

281
00:17:38,030 --> 00:17:38,510
Oh, please.

282
00:17:38,510 --> 00:17:40,750
Because they've got enough kick.

